From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:44:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 149/160] hjviewer: desktop settings split into the everyday
 tabs and Advanced settings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner's 1.9.1 decision (2026-10-26): the desktop settings show the
everyday rows on Account, General, Security and Display, and the expert
rows on a new tab, "Advanced settings" (고급 설정), between the printer
tab and About. Upstream's Network tab is gone; its card is in the new
tab. Placement only: no option key, default or condition changes.

- General keeps the theme, the language, confirm before closing tabs,
  open connections in new tabs and keep awake during outgoing sessions.
- Security keeps the password card (without the numeric one-time
  password), the automatic disconnect with its timeout, the
  connection-window rule and the incoming connections.
- Display keeps the view style, the three image quality presets and
  three default options (remote cursor, mute, lock after session end).
  A custom quality shows as a selected line "Custom (advanced settings)"
  that cannot be picked; the custom choice and its sliders are in the
  new tab.
- Advanced settings has six groups (HjvAdvancedGroup, in
  hjviewer_settings_split.dart): connection (hole punching, IPv6, WebRTC
  and its relay delay, the port forwarding mux, then the network card
  behind the network unlock), display and performance, session
  defaults (the other default options and the toolbar, monitor switch,
  clipboard and note rows, the scroll style, the trackpad speed),
  recording, security (permissions, the numeric one-time password,
  RDP, LAN discovery, direct IP, the whitelists, keep awake, PIN, 2FA
  and the ID, behind the Security tab's unlock; then the audio input
  and the privacy mode implementation, unlocked as before) and the
  service, the updates and Wayland.

Each row shows under the condition of the tab it came from: the new
tab builds the General and Display rows through mixins of their former
State classes, and the Security and Network blocks as embedded widgets.
The security and network unlocks moved to the settings page's state,
so unlocking the Security tab or the new tab's security cards unlocks
both, for as long as the settings page is open, as before.

The home's "Change ID" opens the new tab; the password pencils still
open Security. ko.rs: the tab and card titles.

Tests: the group order, the default options' places against consts.dart
and the Korean titles; the account-first order with the new tab list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
